"citation_ids":["cite.short.res-weighted-support","duverneytachiya"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.short.res-weighted-support"],"id":"short.res-weighted-support","kind":"goal","label":"Theorem 1.2 (a weighted condition on the support)","locator":"Short paper Theorem 1.2, p. 2, label res:weighted-support","source_id":"paper.short.pdf","statement":"*Let $b\\ge2$ be an integer, let $A\\subseteq\\mathbb{N}_{>0}$ be infinite, and let $P$ be a finite nonempty set of primes. Set $h(a)=\\prod_{p\\in P}p^{v_p(a)}$. If\n$$\n\n\n W_{b,P}(A):=\\sum_{a\\in A}\n \\frac{h(a)}{a(b^{h(a)}-1)}<\\infty,\n$$\nthen $X_A(b)$ is irrational. In particular, the base-two condition\n$$\n\n\n \\sum_{a\\in A}\\frac{h(a)}{a(2^{h(a)}-1)}<\\infty\n \\tag{W}\n$$\nimplies that $X_A(b)$ is irrational for every integer $b\\ge2$. Both conclusions are hereditary under passage to infinite subsets.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/nodes/short.res-weighted-support","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/nodes/short.res-reciprocal-support","id":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/edges/%5B%22short.res-reciprocal-support%22%2C%22short.res-weighted-support%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","kind":"supports","record_ref":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/edges/%5B%22short.res-reciprocal-support%22%2C%22short.res-weighted-support%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","semantic_class":"curated_argument_support","to":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/nodes/short.res-weighted-support"},{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/nodes/short.res-weighted-support","id":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/edges/%5B%22short.res-weighted-support%22%2C%22lean.ErdosPr